{
  "manufacturer": "Eastron",
  "model": "SDM230-Modbus",
  "short_model": "SDM230-Modbus",
  "aliases": [
    "SDM230Modbus",
    "SDM230-2T",
    "SDM230-M"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Energy meter",
  "applies_to": "Eastron SDM230-Modbus (two-tariff SDM230-2T protocol) single-phase two-module DIN-rail meter, protocol V1.1.",
  "summary": "The SDM230-Modbus is a single-phase, two-module DIN-rail kWh meter with an RS485 Modbus RTU port and two tariffs. Live values and energy counters, including per-tariff energy and maximum demand, are IEEE-754 floats in input register pairs (function 04). Holding registers cover address, baud, parity, pulse output and the energy measurement mode.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "Modicon",
    "note": "The tables print 30001/40001-style numbers (six-digit 46xxxx for the F0xx/F9xx block) beside the hex start address sent on the wire, e.g. 30073 = 0x0048 and 463777 = 0xF920. Wire address = printed number minus 30001, 40001 or 400001."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "Eastron SDM230Modbus Protocol V1.1 (SDM230-2T Smart Meter Modbus Protocol Implementation)",
    "doc_number": "V1.1",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/fastron-electronics/image/upload/v1619064123/Eastron%20Europe/SDM230-MODBUS_Protocol.pdf",
    "pages": "Input and holding register tables, PDF pp. 2-6"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Word order: the document states floats are sent most significant register first by default, and its read example returns 43 66 33 34 for 230.2 V. All floats here are ABCD. The 'Register Order' register it mentions has no address in the document.",
    "Several register names in the source are printed only in Chinese (demand registers 30085-30095, 30259, 30265 and the 461457 reset); they are translated here.",
    "Source host: the PDF is served from the media store used by Eastron Europe (Fastron Electronics, Eastron's UK distributor) for its product pages.",
    "Left out: 462721 (demand interval / slide time / scroll / backlight), which is a 4-byte BCD packed field.",
    "30387 'Current resettable total reactive energy' is printed with unit kWh; kept as printed, flagged in its description.",
    "The library's separate SDM230-DI file covers the newer DI variant from a different manual."
  ],
